{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"decoder","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decoding allocates a page table entry for every page of 1024 positions from the first listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position to the end, and a page for each page holding a listed element; positions before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first listed one cost nothing. An end is implausible when that span is more than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × count + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages, where ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the number of vertices (or edges) listed: at most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"16 page table entries per listed element (about 2 KB for a vertex, 256 bytes for an edge)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus 64. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"vertexEnd\": 4611686018427387903","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no vertices decodes, in O(1), while a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"payload cannot make decoding allocate without limit. A graph that has run more than that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many empty pages past its live elements does not round-trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/StableGraphs\/documentation\/StableGraphs\/StableDirectedGraph\/init(from:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLang